    "effect_on_the_import": "NONE. Every one of the 23 files under +frozen/ still hashes exactly to its recorded sha256_imported, so the solver this repository runs is bit-for-bit the audited one. Nothing in analysis/OlhoffM4Reconstruction changed.",
    "verification_basis": "Provenance is proved from evidence held inside this repository, and needs no access to the external directory: (1) INTEGRITY -- every +frozen/ file hashes to sha256_imported; (2) ATTESTATION -- for every file but the one declared modification the manifest records sha256_imported == sha256_source, so byte-identity to the audited source is attested by the record; (3) RECONSTRUCTION -- patches/olhoffOpt.m.source-verbatim hashes to the recorded sha256_source (c6c4862440208c2e...), and applying patches/olhoffOpt.timing-instrumentation.diff to it reproduces +frozen/algo/olhoffOpt.m (f83b468415cdeccf...) byte for byte. Check (3) is machine-verified on every run by olhoffm4_apply_unified_diff.m; it is strictly stronger than the external-source comparison it replaces, because it exhibits the delta from the audited source rather than asserting that one exists.",
    "why_this_is_not_a_run_blocker": "The external directory is unversioned, outside this repository and not under its control. A rollback there cannot change which code this repository executes, so it must not decide whether this repository may execute it. Before 2026-09-04 confbench_preflight treated a source-hash difference as fatal; it now records the external state as a preflight NOTE and gates on integrity, attestation and reconstruction instead. The external state is still measured on every run and written into every benchmark manifest.",
